{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdProductConvergence","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdDivisor","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdOrderNeTop","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Analytic.IsolatedZeros","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Analytic.Uniqueness","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Meromorphic.Order"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation.phiBProd_eventually_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation.phiBProd_eventually_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdZeroIsolation.lean#L113-L118","doc":"**`phiBProd`'s zeros are isolated** (branch `Im b² > 0`): `∀ z, ∀ᶠ w in 𝓝[≠] z,\nphiBProd b w ≠ 0`. This discharges the `hΦ₂_iso` input of the G5 uniqueness assembly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation.phiBProd_order_ne_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation.phiBProd_order_ne_top","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdZeroIsolation.lean#L106-L111","doc":"**`phiBProd`'s order is finite everywhere** (branch `Im b² > 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation.den_order_ne_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation.den_order_ne_top","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdZeroIsolation.lean#L93-L104","doc":"The denominator product has order ≠ ⊤ everywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation.num_order_ne_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation.num_order_ne_top","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdZeroIsolation.lean#L79-L91","doc":"The numerator product has order ≠ ⊤ everywhere: entire and (via the `z = 0` witness) not\nidentically zero, so not locally zero at any `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation.denFactor_zero_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation.denFactor_zero_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdZeroIsolation.lean#L58-L77","doc":"Each denominator factor is nonzero at `z = 0` (modular-dual sign). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation.numFactor_zero_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdZeroIsolation.numFactor_zero_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdZeroIsolation.lean#L39-L56","doc":"Each numerator factor is nonzero at `z = 0`: the exponent's real part\n`−π·Im(b²)·(2k+1) < 0`, so `‖exp‖ < 1 = ‖−1‖`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}